      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "All syntheses were performed under aerobic conditions. Mn(NO3)2 (aq., 50%, 0.36 ml, 1.5 mmol) and Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (1.0 mmol; Ln = La for 1) were added to a colorless stirred solution of hmpH (0.10 ml, 1.0 mmol) and NEt3 (0.14 ml, 1.0 mmol) in MeCN (20 ml) and EtOH (5 ml), giving a rapid color change to dark red. The solution was stirred for another 1 h at room temperature, then solid benzoic acid (0.12 g, 1.0 mmol) was added under vigorous stirring. The mixture was stirred for a further 4 h, filtered, and left undisturbed. Slow evaporation at room temperature gave large black crystals in one week, which were collected by filtration, washed thoroughly with MeCN, and dried in vacuum.",
